                <pb facs="0559" n="443" sameAs="frus:frus1923v01/pg443"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.51/175: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Cottrell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">La
                                Paz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-04-06T17:00:00-04:32"><hi rendition="#italic">April 6, 1923—5
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 6:45 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>20. Referring to the Department’s telegram of April 3, 1 p.m. Accompanied by
                    Secretary of Legation Flack had very agreeable conference with the President
                    this afternoon setting forth points in Department’s telegram. President said he
                    had contract and all facts before him and knew the situation and was glad to
                    have the views of the bankers.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cottrell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
